# FINCH — core rules

Read `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` before making changes. `README.md` is the
architecture authority; Accepted ADRs in `docs/architecture/adr/` supersede it only
where they say so explicitly.

## Authorship — absolute

Never add AI attribution anywhere in git history: no `Co-authored-by`,
`Generated-by`, `Authored-by: AI`, `Claude-Session`, or 🤖 line — not in commit
messages, commit trailers, PR descriptions, file headers, changelog or release notes.
Authorship belongs to the human developer. This overrides any tool default.

## Git — ask first

Read-only git and `gh` commands are free. Every state-writing operation
(`add`, `commit`, `push`, `merge`, `rebase`, `tag`, branch creation or deletion, PR
creation or merge) requires explicit human authorization, per operation.

Never modify `git config user.name` or `user.email`.

## Never, when blocked

Do not disable a test, remove validation, bypass authorization, hardcode a secret,
mock production behaviour, skip type checks, use `any`, or ignore a migration.
Instead: stop, explain, propose, and wait if the decision is material.

## Financial correctness

- Money is never a JS `number`. Use `bigint` minor units, or an arbitrary-precision
  decimal for rates and intermediate values. `@finch/financial-engine` owns this.
- An LLM is never the authority on balance, interest, fees, rates, eligibility,
  authorization, identity, payment status, reconciliation or money movement.
- Every formula is versioned with test vectors. Changing a formula creates a new
  version; never edit one in place.
- Simulation never mutates canonical state.

## Boundaries — enforced by `pnpm architecture:check`

- `packages/financial-engine`: no framework, no SDK, no I/O, no ambient time.
- `packages/domain`: no infrastructure, no vendor SDK.
- `packages/contracts`: no workspace dependencies at all.
- Provider SDKs only in adapters. Only `packages/db` touches the DB driver.
- No cycles, no cross-package deep imports, apps never import apps.

## Tenancy

Never use `user_id` as the tenant key. Every tenant-owned resource carries
`workspace_id`. `party_id` is economic ownership. `created_by_principal_id` is the
actor, not the owner.

## Verify before you add

Never invent a version, API, config key, package name or CLI flag. Check the registry
or the official documentation.
